                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "06f515c3-86fd-4c64-81e7-470cfca90710",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa0ea681-dc68-35ac-9185-f507e3bd9228",
                        "source_sense_id": "ea4460ea-0802-3cf8-a471-1340186b9a71",
                        "source_sense_description": "schildpad uit de familie Emydidae",
                        "target_lang_word": "terrapin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "terrapin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1227c9f3-77cb-3e58-87fa-589bf65764fd",
                                        "entry_id": "36073464-5284-3527-9d02-8169a1124cff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several small turtles of the families Emydidae and Geoemydidae found throughout the world."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fdaefdf1-a264-372b-a767-368ac6ce2198",
                                        "entry_id": "36073464-5284-3527-9d02-8169a1124cff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any turtle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7a8bbef-ac1f-470e-8912-a3898c304280",
                                                "sense_id": "fdaefdf1-a264-372b-a767-368ac6ce2198",
                                                "text": "The third ſervice was made up of a loin of freſh pork with apple-ſauce, a kid ſmothered with onions, and a terrapin baked in the ſhell; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ac38901-20ae-479b-b3d9-8092099933b3",
                                                "sense_id": "fdaefdf1-a264-372b-a767-368ac6ce2198",
                                                "text": "The land-turtle, or terrapin, is much better known at Nice, as being a native of this county; yet the beſt are brought from the iſland of Sardinia. The ſoup or bouillon of this animal is always preſcribed here as a great reſtorative to conſumptive patients."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2252917f-7d2a-443c-b4ae-4a427e0f05a0",
                                                "sense_id": "fdaefdf1-a264-372b-a767-368ac6ce2198",
                                                "text": "The ancient whale-cry [i.e., \"town-ho\"] upon first sighting a whale from the masthead, still used by whalemen in hunting the famous Gallipagos terrapin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d52a587b-77a2-35a2-a304-13b55e426a72",
                                        "entry_id": "36073464-5284-3527-9d02-8169a1124cff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several small turtles native to North America that live in brackish or fresh water, especially the diamondback terrapin (Malaclemys terrapin)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f7d0138-d848-44bb-909f-57055b7d329f",
                                                "sense_id": "d52a587b-77a2-35a2-a304-13b55e426a72",
                                                "text": "As to the terrapin, I have not so much to say. The terrapin is a small turtle, found on the shores of Maryland and Virginia, out of which a very rich soup is made. It is cooked with wines and spices, and is served in the shape of a hash, with heaps of little bones mixed through it. […] I must, however, confess that the terrapin for me had no surpassing charms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db2197aa-20b8-36e8-92fc-d638e78ed4ce",
                                        "entry_id": "36073464-5284-3527-9d02-8169a1124cff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The flesh of such a turtle used as food."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8abbcbf8-f76d-4b0b-8ca5-ff0c103bc543",
                                                "sense_id": "db2197aa-20b8-36e8-92fc-d638e78ed4ce",
                                                "text": "The man who did not eat twice of terrapin would be held in small repute, as the Londoner is held who at a city banquet does not partake of both thick and thin turtle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
